{"slug":"time-to-buy-tickets","title":"Time Needed to Buy Tickets","topic":"linear","difficulty":"easy","order":326,"tags":["queue","simulation"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"Simulate a line where people go back to the end","body":["In this line, the person at the front buys **one** ticket per second. If they still want more tickets they go to the **back** of the line; if they are done they leave. This is exactly what a queue does: `popleft` takes the front person, `append` sends them to the back.",{"code":"queue = deque(range(n)); time = 0\nwhile True:\n    i = queue.popleft()\n    need[i] -= 1\n    time += 1\n    if need[i] == 0:\n        if i == k: break        # the person we follow is done\n    else:\n        queue.append(i)         # back to the end of the line"},"Store the **index** of the person in the queue (not their ticket count), so that you know who is who. Simulation is simple and correct; with large numbers of tickets it would be too slow, and a counting formula is needed, but here the sizes are small."]},"statement":["People stand in a line, person `i` wants `tickets[i]` tickets. Every second, the person at the front buys one ticket. If they want more tickets, they go to the back of the line; otherwise they leave. Print the number of seconds until the person at position `k` (counting from 0) has bought all their tickets."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n` and `k`.","The second line has `tickets[0] ... tickets[n-1]`."],"outputFormat":["Print the number of seconds."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","0 <= k < n","1 <= tickets[i] <= 1000"],"examples":[{"input":"3 2\n2 3 2\n","output":"6\n","note":"After 6 seconds: person 2 buys the last ticket in the 6th second."}],"hints":["Put the indexes of the people in a queue.","Take the front person, reduce their need by one and count one second.","If they still need tickets, send them to the back; stop when person k has finished."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn, k = map(int, input().split())\ntickets = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <queue>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    vector<long long> tickets(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> tickets[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] tickets = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < tickets.length; i++) tickets[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["The queue holds the indexes of the people. Each second the front person buys one ticket and either leaves or goes to the back; the simulation stops when person `k` leaves."],"complexity":"Time O(sum of tickets), space O(n).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn, k = map(int, input().split())\ntickets = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nfrom collections import deque\nneed = tickets[:]\nqueue = deque(range(n))\ntime = 0\nwhile True:\n    i = queue.popleft()\n    need[i] -= 1\n    time += 1\n    if need[i] == 0:\n        if i == k:\n            break\n    else:\n        queue.append(i)\nprint(time)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <queue>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    long long k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    vector<long long> tickets(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> tickets[i];\n\n    vector<long long> need = tickets;\n    queue<int> line;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) line.push(i);\n    long long time = 0;\n    while (true) {\n        int i = line.front();\n        line.pop();\n        need[i]--;\n        time++;\n        if (need[i] == 0) {\n            if (i == k) break;\n        } else {\n            line.push(i);\n        }\n    }\n    cout << time << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long k = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] tickets = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < tickets.length; i++) tickets[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        long[] need = tickets.clone();\n        Deque<Integer> line = new ArrayDeque<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) line.addLast(i);\n        long time = 0;\n        while (true) {\n            int i = line.pollFirst();\n            need[i]--;\n            time++;\n            if (need[i] == 0) {\n                if (i == k) break;\n            } else {\n                line.addLast(i);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(time);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"3 2\n2 3 2\n","output":"6\n"},{"input":"1 0\n5\n","output":"5\n"},{"input":"3 0\n5 1 1\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"3 2\n1 1 5\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"10 4\n5 4 2 3 5 3 6 7 2 7\n","output":"36\n"},{"input":"300 150\n27 67 92 99 30 5 61 56 58 55 75 84 10 63 27 34 41 6 92 47 3 48 95 87 41 29 87 9 54 1 12 65 27 19 37 65 91 53 26 79 75 58 91 35 23 43 66 20 11 56 38 31 3 5 56 47 16 100 77 40 33 21 78 80 87 7 59 89 45 80 58 90 31 48 17 32 70 65 11 51 3 73 3 16 61 79 99 55 51 76 54 96 67 75 22 52 82 4 93 34 26 74 48 60 93 62 89 67 36 81 11 73 34 79 93 97 2 43 56 10 10 56 2 53 65 9 89 60 42 10 3 58 67 69 32 77 72 23 62 57 33 72 88 27 89 6 69 17 64 66 93 92 97 5 50 20 18 52 92 68 11 34 3 24 65 99 4 64 7 31 100 99 58 57 38 35 36 57 17 89 20 24 18 97 25 58 43 25 10 69 9 70 5 49 1 22 35 37 96 55 70 97 45 58 25 44 83 4 98 45 86 43 33 38 62 38 90 35 24 46 57 12 73 22 100 84 2 65 91 41 21 92 99 75 18 54 94 41 61 52 12 3 29 21 3 82 88 87 76 40 95 35 70 63 63 10 19 45 7 42 57 66 12 74 57 47 79 19 79 81 18 77 4 71 60 69 4 11 42 13 69 40 49 59 13 41 67 9 62 20 37 30 44 20 10 23 67 9 96 77\n","output":"14650\n"},{"input":"1000 0\n206 225 924 869 878 932 442 325 811 365 360 979 456 240 901 791 526 716 109 957 971 839 477 644 441 432 60 845 80 369 434 3 861 612 903 510 622 740 352 798 464 294 584 817 544 726 617 266 775 181 639 179 72 320 811 226 424 965 312 363 851 691 851 86 613 495 74 825 440 397 958 447 348 347 537 827 952 244 100 798 447 724 775 280 47 76 61 75 30 753 871 642 487 865 167 855 812 789 202 110 553 646 111 772 678 282 466 750 826 14 606 295 377 767 608 872 678 22 918 486 707 722 507 559 998 313 87 477 945 153 433 60 438 433 678 197 38 966 522 986 405 701 411 568 119 953 319 199 941 66 225 373 9 722 240 118 728 872 839 353 382 137 499 221 395 372 995 387 344 930 758 981 99 483 398 730 456 962 509 970 422 48 474 275 558 172 531 540 411 74 717 993 909 671 994 888 602 778 817 350 209 110 21 737 433 582 23 712 442 984 568 793 526 979 116 127 845 66 667 862 87 950 902 478 635 834 97 664 867 281 62 895 456 31 379 322 977 137 905 214 790 370 500 521 717 592 597 683 484 803 265 514 920 405 676 156 9 692 939 373 463 901 705 73 957 320 398 902 8